# Frantic Scapegoat: "Whenever one or more other creatures you control enter, if this creature is suspected, you may suspect one of the
# other creatures" (CR 603.2c, 701.60a). A Dragon Fodder makes two Goblin tokens at once: that is one trigger, not two, and Bot1
# suspects exactly one of the two Goblins (it cannot pick both; the other is not), while the Scapegoat is no longer suspected.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Dragon Fodder
Frantic Scapegoat
Plains x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Frantic Scapegoat.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Suspected = true
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dragon Fodder.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
! Bot1.Choose(Goblin Token#1; Goblin Token#2)
Bot1.Choose(Goblin Token#2)

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Frantic Scapegoat.Suspected = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#2.Suspected = true
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Suspected = (absent)
Bot1.Battlefield.Goblin Token#1.Keywords = (absent)
